# =============================================================================
# ASSESSMENT SOURCE MATERIAL — kept on the Desktop, never pushed
# =============================================================================
# These are the submitted CA1/CA2 documents, the architecture diagram, the progress
# deck, and the weekly report template. They contain the student ID, the student email
# address, and an Academic Integrity Certificate Verification Code.
#
# That verification code is the credential used to confirm a submission is the
# candidate's own work. It must not be published, so these files stay out of git
# entirely — not just out of the working tree, but out of history.
#
# The Desktop copy is the primary record and stays where it is.
# `docs/source_material/MANIFEST.md` documents what is excluded and why.
Practicum_CA1 submission.pdf
Practicum CA2 Submission.docx
*Weekly Activity Report Template.docx
architecture diagram.drawio.pdf
From-Problem-to-Prototype.pptx
*.docx
*.pptx
source_material/

# =============================================================================
# SECRETS — never commit. Checked before every push.
# =============================================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
credentials/
.openai_api_key
*_api_key*
*_apikey*
service-account*.json
gha-creds-*.json

# Participant data. This project has no human-participant data during the current
# phase, and must not acquire any before ethics approval is confirmed.
# If this pattern ever matches a real file, that is an ethics incident, not a
# gitignore problem — stop and report it.
data/participants/
data/raw/participants/
*participant*responses*
*participant*identifiers*
*consent*records*
anonymised/
pseudonymised/

# =============================================================================
# PYTHON
# =============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# =============================================================================
# SECRETS IN NOTEBOOKS
# =============================================================================
# Strip outputs before committing any notebook, so a key pasted into a cell
# during exploration cannot be published by accident.
*.ipynb_checkpoints
.ipynb_output/

# =============================================================================
# LOCAL DATABASES AND VECTOR STORES
# =============================================================================
# Chroma and similar stores are rebuildable from the corpus plus the embedding
# cache, so they are not committed. The *inputs* that define them are.
chroma/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
chroma.sqlite3
.pgdata/

# =============================================================================
# LARGE / REGENERABLE ARTEFACTS
# =============================================================================
# Embedding caches are large and fully rebuildable from the corpus + model name.
# They are also the artefact most likely to silently drift from the corpus version,
# so keeping them out of git is safer than versioning them.
embeddings_cache/
*.npy
*.npz
*.faiss
*.bin
.cache/

# Note: the synthetic corpus, query set, ground truth and experiment results are
# deliberately NOT ignored. Reproducibility requires them to be version-controlled
# alongside the code that produced them. Only caches and secrets are excluded.

# =============================================================================
# OPERATING SYSTEM
# =============================================================================
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

